## What Problem This Solves

`clampSessionCaptureText` and `clampSessionCaptureTitle` in `ui/src/lib/workboard/index.ts` use raw `compact.slice(0, MAX - 3)` to truncate workboard capture previews. When `MAX - 3` is odd (697 for text, 177 for title) and an emoji (UTF-16 surrogate pair) sits exactly on that boundary, the `slice` leaves a dangling high surrogate — producing garbled text (`�`) on the Workboard card.

`truncateUtf16Safe` is already imported in this file (added by #101685 for `buildCardSessionLabel`) but was not applied to these two remaining raw-`slice` codepaths.

## Why This Change Was Made

Replace the two remaining raw `.slice(0, N - 3)` calls with `truncateUtf16Safe(compact, N - 3)` so surrogate-pair integrity is preserved at the truncation boundary. This completes the UTF-16 hardening in this file — #101685 fixed `buildCardSessionLabel`, this PR fixes the other two truncation sites.

## User Impact

Workboard cards with emoji near the capture text/title boundaries no longer display garbled `�` characters. No other behavior change.

## Evidence

**Real environment tested:** local OpenClaw source checkout, Node v24.13.1, PR head.

**Proof — real `truncateUtf16Safe` import via `node --import tsx`:**

The actual functions `clampSessionCaptureText` and `clampSessionCaptureTitle` are private (not exported), so the evidence exercises the same production helper (`truncateUtf16Safe` from `@openclaw/normalization-core/utf16-slice`) that the fix uses, at the exact boundary values matching the source constants (`SESSION_CAPTURE_TEXT_MAX_CHARS - 3 = 697`, `WORKBOARD_CAPTURE_TITLE_MAX_CHARS - 3 = 177`):

```
$ node --import tsx -e "
import { truncateUtf16Safe } from '@openclaw/normalization-core/utf16-slice';

const MAX_TEXT = 700;
const MAX_TITLE = 180;

// --- Text boundary (697 = MAX_TEXT - 3) ---
const s1 = 'x'.repeat(MAX_TEXT - 4) + '😀';
const bad = s1.slice(0, MAX_TEXT - 3);
const good = truncateUtf16Safe(s1, MAX_TEXT - 3);
console.log('=== Text boundary:', MAX_TEXT - 3, '===');
console.log('BEFORE .slice:        len=' + bad.length,  ' lone surrogate=' + (bad.charCodeAt(bad.length - 1) >= 0xD800));
console.log('AFTER  truncateUtf16: len=' + good.length, ' lone surrogate=' + (good.charCodeAt(good.length - 1) >= 0xD800));

// --- Title boundary (177 = MAX_TITLE - 3) ---
const s2 = 'x'.repeat(MAX_TITLE - 4) + '😀';
const bad2 = s2.slice(0, MAX_TITLE - 3);
const good2 = truncateUtf16Safe(s2, MAX_TITLE - 3);
console.log('');
console.log('=== Title boundary:', MAX_TITLE - 3, '===');
console.log('BEFORE .slice:        len=' + bad2.length,  ' lone surrogate=' + (bad2.charCodeAt(bad2.length - 1) >= 0xD800));
console.log('AFTER  truncateUtf16: len=' + good2.length, ' lone surrogate=' + (good2.charCodeAt(good2.length - 1) >= 0xD800));
"
=== Text boundary: 697 ===
BEFORE .slice:        len=697  lone surrogate=true
AFTER  truncateUtf16: len=696  lone surrogate=false

=== Title boundary: 177 ===
BEFORE .slice:        len=177  lone surrogate=true
AFTER  truncateUtf16: len=176  lone surrogate=false
```

**Observed result after fix:** In the text boundary case (697), `truncateUtf16Safe` drops the lone high surrogate and returns 696 chars of intact text instead of 697 chars with a broken emoji. In the title boundary case (177), same behavior — 176 chars intact instead of 177 with a broken emoji. Both boundary values match the actual source constants.

**What was not tested:** The actual `clampSessionCaptureText`/`clampSessionCaptureTitle` end-to-end on a running Gateway with real Workboard cards. The fix is a direct helper swap at static boundary values; the helper's surrogate-safe behavior is proven independently.

## Regression Test Plan

- `$ git diff --check` — clean ✅
- `$ git diff --stat` — **1 file, +2/-2** ✅
- `truncateUtf16Safe` import already present from #101685; no new dependencies
- Focused regression coverage is provided by `packages/normalization-core/src/utf16-slice.test.ts`

## Root Cause

In `clampSessionCaptureText` (line 2912) and `clampSessionCaptureTitle` (line 2920), `compact.slice(0, MAX - 3)` operates on UTF-16 code units. When `SESSION_CAPTURE_TEXT_MAX_CHARS - 3 = 697` or `WORKBOARD_CAPTURE_TITLE_MAX_CHARS - 3 = 177` (both odd), an emoji sitting on the boundary gets its high surrogate included but its low surrogate dropped, producing a dangling surrogate pair and garbled display text. The fix uses `truncateUtf16Safe` — already imported in this file by #101685 — which detects surrogate pairs at the boundary and adjusts the slice point to avoid splitting them.

